[size=5][b]Download the main file on this page[/b][/size]
The editor is a standalone program (MW5SaveEditor.exe) that you run yourself; it never connects to the internet. Download [b]MechWarrior5.SaveEditor-<version>.zip[/b] from the Files tab, extract it anywhere and run MW5SaveEditor.exe. The same zip is mirrored on [url=https://github.com/mindattic/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor/releases/latest]GitHub[/url], with the source code.

[size=5][b]Description[/b][/size]
One save editor for [b]MechWarrior 5: Mercenaries[/b] and [b]MechWarrior 5: Clans[/b], built from scratch around three ideas: never risk your saves, do in one click what used to take fifty, and look like it belongs in the game. Switch games with the tabs at the top; each keeps its own open save. The same download is on both pages: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mechwarrior5mercenaries/mods/1666]Mercenaries[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mechwarrior5clans/mods/70]Clans[/url].

[size=5][b]Links[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Documentation:[/b] [url=https://mindattic.github.io/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor/]mindattic.github.io/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor[/url] ([url=https://mindattic.github.io/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor/docs/USER_GUIDE.html]user guide[/url])
[*][b]Source code:[/b] [url=https://github.com/mindattic/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor]github.com/mindattic/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor[/url] (issues and feedback welcome)
[/list]

[size=5][b]Both games[/b][/size]
[b]Pick saves by name, not by GUID[/b]
Campaigns and saves are listed by their in-game names, with dates and the details that matter; autosaves are marked. Double-click to open.

[b]'Mech pictures from your own game, and Sarna.net links[/b]
Pictures are read from your installed game files, never downloaded. Every 'Mech also has a link that opens its Sarna.net page in your browser, for its full technical specs.

[b]Compatibility report[/b]
Opening a save lists everything in it that isn't vanilla, with the mod behind it, its version and page, or why that mod isn't active (not installed, turned off, wrong version).

[b]One look per game: Mercs amber and Clans ice[/b]
A gunmetal and amber look for Mercenaries and a cold steel and ice-cyan look for Clans, modeled on the games' own menus; it follows the game tab. Batch buttons stay greyed out until something is ticked, so an action only touches what you see. Six languages: English, Deutsch, Español, Français, 日本語, Русский.

[size=5][b]MechWarrior 5: Mercenaries[/b][/size]
[b]Requisition: tick, shift-click, add[/b]
Every 'Mech variant through [b]DLC 9: Ashes & Ascension[/b], plus those your mods add, with tonnage, class, hero name, DLC source and how many you own. Tick any number (Shift+click for a range, Ctrl+A for everything shown) and [b]add them all to cold storage[/b] in one click, copies included. Each arrives with its real factory loadout and paint. Filter by weight class, heroes, DLC pack, owned DLC only, or search by code, chassis or hero name.

[b]Mech Lab: hardpoint-aware refits[/b]
Double-click a hangar 'Mech to refit it. Each hardpoint offers only the weapons that fit it (energy, ballistic, missile, AMS, omni, melee) at every tier, with weapon groups kept. Front and rear armor per location against the variant's maximum, equipment slots that offer only what fits, 'Mech traits, and builds you can export and import as [b].mw5loadout[/b] files. A damaged 'Mech keeps its damage until you repair it.

[b]Company[/b]
C-Bills (+1M / +10M / +100M / Max), reputation, company name, and the campaign date: moving it moves payroll, injuries and contracts with it. Cantina career paths (points, level, next reward) and Arena fame with its rank, all read from the game's own data and your mods'. Export a whole company and import it into another campaign: its 'Mechs arrive repaired and its pilots healthy.

[b]Inventory[/b]
Any weapon, equipment or ammo at any tier, in bulk, optionally with each weapon's ammo added too (paired by the game's own ammo types). Set counts for many stacks at once, or remove them.

[b]Pilots[/b]
Hire pilots with the selected pilot's skills, as a rookie, or with random skills; release them; edit name, callsign, persona, portrait, voice, bio, traits, skill caps and XP. Heal all, max all caps.

[b]Factions[/b]
Standing from -100 to +100 (or what your mods allow) for every faction, or set them all allied or neutral.

[size=5][b]MechWarrior 5: Clans[/b][/size]
[b]Resources: Kerenskies, Honor, salvage, crew, MXP[/b]
Set Kerenskies, Merits and Honor (Honor also moves the Honor level track, which follows the game's own Honor ladder), mech, weapon and equipment components, technicians, scientists, crew upgrades, and per-chassis mech experience. Quick +10 / +100 / +1K buttons on every value.

[b]Mechs: your whole Touman at a glance[/b]
Every 'Mech with its variant, tonnage, installed gear and condition. Tick 'Mechs (Shift+click, Select all, or [b]Select damaged[/b]) to [b]repair[/b], [b]duplicate[/b] (same loadout, fully repaired), [b]rename[/b] or [b]remove[/b] them; any deployed in your Star or in the mech bay's work queue are kept. Filter by name, chassis, variant or weapon.

[b]Weapons, equipment and progress[/b]
Edit your stock and requisition any weapon or piece of equipment seen in Clans campaigns, in bulk. Honor level and experience, cycles elapsed, the technician pool, the research queue and completed research.

[b]Clans pictures[/b]
Clans keeps its 'Mech pictures Oodle-compressed. If an Oodle DLL (oo2core*.dll, Epic's decompression library, for example from an Unreal Engine install) is already on your PC, the editor uses it to show Clans' own pictures; it never downloads or bundles one. Otherwise each 'Mech shows the Mercenaries picture of the same chassis, or its initials.

[size=5][b]Mod support[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Every installed mod is read from its own files[/b] when the editor starts (Mods folder and Steam Workshop, in the game's load order), with no per-mod code. A new or updated mod that uses the game's own data (weapons, equipment, ammo, traits, 'Mechs, the pilot skill curve, career paths, ammo types, fame ranks) is followed without an editor update; with Pilot Overhaul - Eternal enabled, skill caps go to 30. Press Rescan in Settings after changing mods.
[*][b]Every limit follows the active mods:[/b] skill cap, XP, salary, C-Bills, faction standing and stack size. A value a save already holds beyond a limit is kept, never forced back.
[*][b]One mod misbehaving?[/b] A small add-on pack (a JSON data file in the Addons folder) fixes or tweaks that mod while it's active: an ammo pairing, a name, a limit. Packs apply only while their mod is installed, enabled and a supported version; packs for AVTA, PilotOverhaul - Eternal, YAW-CE, the YASV patch and Yet Another Mechlab are included. Report a problem on [url=https://github.com/mindattic/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor/issues]GitHub[/url] with the mod's name and version.
[*][b]Limits:[/b] a mod that changes rules only in its code leaves no data to read. Clans mods are recognized by name and traced in the compatibility report; their detailed stats aren't read yet. Chain fire, the quest log and moving 'Mechs in or out of the active bay aren't offered (their save layouts couldn't be verified).
[/list]

[size=5][b]Your saves are safe[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]An original game save is [b]never overwritten[/b]. Saving writes a new save beside it and adds it to the game's load menu under the name you choose. The original stays byte-for-byte identical.
[*]Saves the editor writes carry a small, harmless marker the game ignores. Only those are ever updated in place, and the previous version is kept as a [b].bak[/b].
[*][b]Lossless or nothing:[/b] if a save can't be reproduced exactly, the editor refuses to edit it instead of guessing.
[*]The game's save index files are backed up before every change.
[*]Tested end to end: an automated suite edits copies of real campaign saves for both games, reopens every written file and checks each change, and edited saves have been loaded and played in both games.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
[b]This is a program you run, not a mod the game loads[/b], so it doesn't need Vortex.
[list=1]
[*]Download [b]MechWarrior5.SaveEditor-<version>.zip[/b] (Manual Download on the Files tab), or the same zip from [url=https://github.com/mindattic/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor/releases/latest]GitHub[/url].
[*]Extract it anywhere, for example your Desktop. Keep everything in the folder together: the exe, the .NET runtime files beside it, and the [b]Addons[/b] folder.
[*]Double-click [b]MW5SaveEditor.exe[/b]. No .NET install is needed.
[/list]

[b]Using it[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Quit the game, or stay on its main menu, so the save you edit isn't in use.
[*]Run [b]MW5SaveEditor.exe[/b] and choose [b]MERCENARIES[/b] or [b]CLANS[/b] at the top. Your saves are listed by name; double-click one to open it.
[*]Make your changes, type a name for the edited save, and press [b]Save as new[/b] (Ctrl+S).
[*]In the game, load the save with that name. Your original save is still there, unchanged.
[/list]

[b]Uninstalling:[/b] delete the folder you extracted. Your settings are the [b]settings.json[/b] beside the exe; the editor writes nothing anywhere else except your saves.

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]MechWarrior 5: Mercenaries and/or MechWarrior 5: Clans on Windows (Steam or Epic). Game Pass / Microsoft Store saves live elsewhere and are untested; use Open to pick them at your own risk.
[*]Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit. The download is self-contained.
[*]No DLC or other mods required. Back up a campaign you care about before editing it, as with any save editor.
[*]No internet access: the program never connects to the internet. It reads only your saves and your game's and mods' files; Sarna.net links open in your own browser only when you click one.
[/list]

